  "explanation": "The sources identify three distinct units named '371st' with different types: 1) The 371st Engineer Construction Battalion (also called 371st Engineer Battalion), activated in 1944 (D1S1, D3S4). 2) The 371st Infantry Regiment (United States), a segregated African American regiment serving in WWI and WWII (D5S1, D7S2). 3) The 371st Bombardment Squadron, which existed in two variants: as a Heavy squadron (D9S6) and as a Medium squadron (D10S1). The original R5 answers missed the specific 'Heavy' and 'Medium' distinctions found in the source texts, which are valid complementary answers for the same entity number. 'Special Service Regiment' and 'General Service Regiment' are designations applied to the Engineer unit, not the primary unit type itself, so they are excluded in favor of the more specific 'Engineer Construction Battalion'. Full names like '371st Infantry Regiment' are collapsed to the requested 'type' (Infantry Regiment)."
